1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,525
A 500-token answer is 500 trips
through the whole model.

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:07,900
The model reads all your tokens.

3
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:13,617
It scores every possible next token, and
turns the scores into probabilities.

4
00:00:14,217 --> 00:00:17,117
It picks one, appends it, and starts over.

5
00:00:18,117 --> 00:00:22,092
Every trip runs all 96 of GPT-3's layers.

6
00:00:22,717 --> 00:00:27,442
And reads 350 GB of weights, for
every single token.

7
00:00:27,742 --> 00:00:31,092
That's why a long answer takes
time, and costs more.
